{"name":"Sphinx","hex":"#a99593","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sphinx","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Sphingidae – many species of moths."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An ancient, large statue in Egypt, with the face of a man and the body of a lion, lying near the Great Pyramids.","One of the many offspring of Typhon and Echidna, a winged lion-like creature with a woman's face, who dwelt near the city of Thebes in Boeotia and terrorized travelers by posing riddles, killing those who failed to answer correctly; after Oedipus solved her riddle, she committed suicide out of frustration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sphinx"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sphinx","blocks":[{"text":"A sphinx is a mythical creature with the head of a human, the body of a lion, and the wings of an eagle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sphinx_CdM_Paris_DeRidder865_n2.jpg/330px-Sphinx_CdM_Paris_DeRidder865_n2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphinx","wikidata":"Q151480"},{"title":"Sphinx (search engine)","blocks":[{"text":"Sphinx is a fulltext search engine that provides text search functionality to client applications."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphinx_(search_engine)","wikidata":"Q984965"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_20080716a.jpg/500px-Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_20080716a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_20080716a.jpg/1280px-Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_20080716a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_20080716a.jpg/500px-Great_Sphinx_of_Giza_-_200